BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Robert O'Hearn's Storytelling through Theatrical Design
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260626T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260626T090000
UID:260506ycTFEOUXPkCQ9sqY5QXJmA
DESCRIPTION:location: Indiana University Archives 1320 E. 10th Street Herm
 an B Wells Library E460 Bloomington\, IN 47405 date/time: 03/23-06/26 9:00
 -5:00 Monday-Friday description: This new exhibition features a variety of
  costume and scenic designs by the late Robert O'Hearn\, alumnus and profe
 ssor emeritus of opera studies in the Jacobs School of Music at Indiana Un
 iversity. O'Hearn also worked as an opera\, ballet\, and theater designer 
 for the Metropolitan Opera\, IU Opera and Ballet Theater\, Broadway\, and 
 other opera and theater companies across the country and Europe. A selecti
 on from the 600\\+ works that are now held by the University Archives cele
 brates O'Hearn as a visual storyteller\, talented artist\, and impactful d
 esigner.
LOCATION:Indiana University - Bloomington
URL:https://guides.idsnews.com/happenings/event/robert-ohearns-storytellin
 g-through-theatrical-design
X-SOURCE:Limestone Post
END:VEVENT
