BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Curiosity Lab
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260702T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260702T174500
UID:260626aUmcvxescE-loNd0E58L-A
DESCRIPTION:July Theme: Scientists Day: Thursday Time: 4 - 5:45pm Recommen
 ded Ages: Designed for children ages 6 - 10\, but siblings are welcome. Lo
 cation: WonderLab Cost: Free for Members / Free with Museum Admission Curi
 osity Lab is an after-school\, free play program for kids ages 6-10 years.
  Children are invited to explore\, experiment\, and engage in hands-on sen
 sory activities at their own pace. No instructions\, no pressure-just curi
 osity-driven play. Held in WonderLab \\(or sometimes outdoors weather perm
 itting\\)\, the space is set up for exploration with a variety of rotating
  materials and stations. There will be one main activity/installment/manip
 ulative for the month that will be brought out every Thursday. This will r
 otate with the month and the month's theme.
LOCATION:Wonderlab
URL:https://wonderlab.org/event/curiosity-lab-8/2026-07-02/
X-SOURCE:Limestone Post
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Science Story Time
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260702T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260702T103000
UID:260626YrF3KlDCt0a6PP3Zyv2XXg
DESCRIPTION:July Theme: Scientists Day: Thursdays Time: 10 - 10:30am Recom
 mended Ages Children ages 2-6 and their caregivers Cost: Free for Members 
 / Free with Museum Admission Science Story Time is geared toward listeners
  toddler through early elementary ages. This program uses children's pictu
 re books to engage as well as support scientific concepts and experiments.
  Young scientists develop literacy and STEM skills as well as build vocabu
 lary by actively participating in the hands-on program. Activities designe
 d for ages 3-6. All are welcome. March activities might include: Reading a
  story about a science fair and conducting a chemical reaction Reading a s
 tory about an underrepresented scientist and learning how science is all a
